# Sample macro file -- template for specifying a material and the
# quantities to compute for it, without going through the interactive menu.
#
# Run:   ./run sample.mac
#
# Copy this file, edit the values below, and point /output/ lines at
# whatever filenames you want. See examples/*.mac for more worked examples
# (all ten CHON project mixtures, plus a single-element case) and
# epixs/macro.py's docstring for the full directive reference.

# --- Material -----------------------------------------------------------
# Option A: a mixture, built from weight fractions of elements or compounds
# (repeat /material/addElement as many times as needed; fractions are
# normalized automatically, so they don't need to already sum to 1).
/material/name SAMPLE
/material/density 1.334335
/material/addElement C 0.514264
/material/addElement H 0.073925
/material/addElement O 0.320019
/material/addElement N 0.082377
/material/addElement S 0.009415

# Option B: a single element or compound -- comment out Option A above and
# uncomment this instead (don't use both at once):
#/material/name Lead
#/material/density 11.35
#/material/formula Pb

# --- Energies / depths ---------------------------------------------------
/energies 0.1,0.5,1.0,2.0,5.0,10.0
/depths 1,5,10,20,40

# --- What to compute (comment out any you don't need) --------------------
/output/massAttenuation sample_mass_attenuation.csv
/output/hvl sample_hvl_tvl_mfp.csv
/output/zeff sample_zeff_zeq.csv
/output/ebf sample_ebf.csv
/output/eabf sample_eabf.csv
/output/neutron sample_neutron.csv
